{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552086-have-you-used-an-antidulivan-in-a-game","id":1552086,"title":"Have you used an antidulivan in a game?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-07-05T16:17:43-07:00","id":1552086,"title":"Have you used an antidulivan in a game?","content":"I'm just curious if there is anyone on the boards that had a member of the 3rd generation make an appearance in your game and was it difficult?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-05T17:01:42-07:00","id":1552089,"title":"","content":"I played in a game where Troile appeared. She incarnated in the form of a AI supercomputer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":26996,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","user":"Amethyst","date":". 07-05-2025, 08:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-05T17:39:03-07:00","id":1552090,"title":"","content":"Interesting take on the Brush antidulivan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-05T20:25:56-07:00","id":1552092,"title":"","content":"We did a &quot;try to cram as many end of the world scenarios together and see what works&quot;.<br /> <br /> So, mixed Ascension, Apocalypse and Gehenna. A bit of the Kuei Jin ending and something for Demon and Mummy.<br /> <br /> Long story short, everyone got what they wanted (thanks to mage ascension for humans, and a mix of the werewolf endings), but the process was traumatic (gehenna, mummies, etc).<br /> <br /> Nearly all of us had a character in a major splat (Mage, Vampire, Werewolf), except a few of us that got Major and some minor, or my case that I got only Mage (late joiner to the game).<br /> <br /> We overlapped scenarios, so when the Tzimisce rose in New York, some Werewolves were there to punch it in the mouth(s). When Lasombra blanketed the earth, a cabal of mages summoned enough sunlight to kill it (and no one but us knew what killed it), Mikaboshi (briefly) became the Demon Emperor, Mummies were throwing a spanner in the works; Mummies ended up causing the Wall to strenghten and fucking up the Kuei Jin but saving the world from the 1000 hells as a side effect; etc.<br /> <br /> I think it was the best thing we ever played and was all over the place because we (players) though we were getting the ALL bad endings, but somehow our ST got us through all of it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-05T22:27:20-07:00","id":1552093,"title":"","content":"In a pre-history/Mythic age, Dark Age or and Antiquity game they tend to appear, just like in a Gehenna/Post-Gehenna games<br /> In a modern era game? I rarely use them unless the Players manage somehow - spoiler: players are quite creative to make their own unlife way shorter than you tend to... - stumble in one<br /> When they are part of the Story? Usually I use Absimilliard, Arikel, Ishtar, Veddhartha, Zapathasura, Saulot, the Eldest, Sutekh, Malkav, Malakai, Nahema and or Set, the Snake (Who I firmly belive is <i>not</i> Sutekh, but a seperate Antediluvian who been active in the Second City. Simply what we know about Set from other clan's stories not really fit the Sutekh story. Set, the Snake, brother of Arikel, Saulot, Malkav, Malakai and Nahema was quie philosophical, but agressive)\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-06T08:58:08-07:00","id":1552103,"title":"","content":"I had an Easter egg one in my city, innana who bothered embracing. She was made by enoch to act as a advisor and Chancellor, following the 1st and second cities she concluded vampires should rule and had spent most of her time observing humanities social developments pretending to be a venture elder borderline autarkis.<br /> <br /> Her discipline lineup is fortitude, presence and auspex. Her clan flaw is her mental disciplines don't work on rulers.<br /> generally she was a very respected noddist scholar which is how most pcs would interact with her","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-06T10:17:15-07:00","id":1552106,"title":"","content":"I had Arikel as an easter egg once. She was actually pretending to be human and working with deliveries, focusing on maintaining her Humanity high, so the PCs did encounter her a lot of times without realizing. Only by the end of the game did a PC realize there was something up with the regular delivery girl and ended up having a scene talking to her about the events in the city and the undead condition in general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-06T10:45:41-07:00","id":1552108,"title":"","content":"I've never used any of the Antediluvians in my chronicles and don't plan to do so. My main concern is how terrifying are we supposed to hold Gehenna if they (even only some of them) are up and about being active in recent times? In order to preserve the mystery and fear that should surround them, they must be unknown. This also means that any 4th generation childer who were not sired in very ancient times, either have their generation reduced to 5th generation or are 4th generation only because of diablerie.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, even canon creates problems for this as we have at least two Antediluvians being active enough that they sired new childer in the Middle Ages and at least one being active and known even as late as the formation of the Camarilla. So I've had to change things from canon in my own chronicles.<br /> <br /> This is how I handle them:<br /> <br /> The Second City was Babel. After Babel fell, the Antediluvians went to their own different cities in Mesopotamia where they became their legendary god-king founders.<br /> <br /> The Antediluvians have more or less been in torpor since 4000-3000 BC. For the most part, all the stories told about them are before this time. There are still some exceptions, and each time there was activity, something important happened.<br /> <br /> Lasombra did wake up some time after this to destroy ALL of his original 4th generation childer and embrace Montano sometime before the Santorini explosion. However, he went back into torpor after he successfully identified his only loyal childe, sired him, educated him, and released him (Montano). I haven't yet decided if he instructed Montano to bring Gratiano to him for some kind of cold embrace, or if he instructed Montano to instead embrace Gratiano himself. In either case, while Montano did not want to do this he obeyed his sire.<br /> <br /> Saulot was briefly active during the time of Classical Rome as he embraced his last childe during the time of Caligula. Some time prior to that is when he discovered and realized Golconda and spread it to some of his childer.<br /> <br /> Cappadocious woke from torpor several times in antiquity, each time corresponding with a great plague. He converted to Christianity during the Antonine plague, and he performed the Feast of Folly during the plague of Justinian. He did not actively sire Augustus, but informed his childe Japheth in dreams to bring Augustus to his torpored body and perform a cold embrace. The manner in which Augustus diablerized Cappadocious is totally different than what is in the Giovanni Chronicles.<br /> <br /> Typhon was active at times in the history of Ancient Egypt, but most of the activity attributed to him at this time was actually his 4th generation childe Set, brother of Osiris. He was active around 900 BC when his forces were mostly annihilated by Horus and the Silent Striders and driven out of Egypt. He destroyed most (but not all) of his surviving clan then and established a new way the clan would organize itself to prevent such a defeat from occurring again.<br /> <br /> Tzimisce briefly woke to defend himself during the Anarch Revolt when he slew his attackers, but went back to torpor soon thereafter.<br /> <br /> Torpor is simply the best survival strategy for the Antediluvians, and it is a necessary phase to both build their powers and conduct the Jyhad on a psychic level. More often than not, when an Antediluvian does waken from torpor, it is an outside event that forces it on them. When it isn't, it's because it is a necessary part of their plan in the Jyhad. In so far they are &quot;active&quot; today, it is not physically active but psychically active despite being in torpor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-06T13:32:10-07:00","id":1552112,"title":"","content":"I think it depends a lot on if and how you want to portray Gehenna in your games (regardless if it'll happen or not). I <b>usually</b> prefer to make it a legend that's ultimately wrong. Whatever the truth is, it's something else the vampiric society doesn't really have a clue about.<br /> <br /> An Antedeluvian in this context may be a lot of things. The only thing the PC learned from my Arikel is that she was extremely old and powerful, but she didn't really talked about the past. While her insight on the vampire condition was relevant to the character, she left far more questions than answers about the Antes.<br /> <br /> She did said Gehenna doesn't exist, but that was a plot point for that particular chronicle regardless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-07T04:36:29-07:00","id":1552135,"title":"","content":"It seems sensible to retain Antediluvians as the Sleeping Giants of the setting, rather than actual NPCs - though some part of me loves the notion that when the Antediluvians ARE active one notices them only with the benefit of hindsight (Since vampires are, after all, shadowy predators who thrive by operating Sub Rosa so it makes sense that any vampire able to live so terrifyingly long are going to be past <i>and</i> present masters of \u201cRun Silent, Run Deep\u201d).<br /> <br /> <br /> As for Gehenna, I\u2019ve gone back and forth on this, but for the moment I tend to side with the notion that Gehenna is mostly the end phase of the vicious cycle that defines vampire existence to this very night - a long game that produces reigning champions and survivors rather than winners or losers.<br /> <br /> Whether this will always be the case, however, should remain an Interesting Question.<br /> <br /> <br /> When it comes to the Garou, however, The Apocalypse is Played For Keeps: a genuine Ragnarok, to gives the long painful struggle a point and a Big Finish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-07T04:38:23-07:00","id":1552136,"title":"","content":"It just struck me that the points above may be driven by my suspicion that World of Darkness vampires - no matter how powerful, feared, charismatic etc - should always be slightly \u2018smaller than life\u2019 to put their rather cruel &amp; solipsistic power games in perspective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-07T11:59:03-07:00","id":1552159,"title":"","content":"I've played one in a game; after reading Ann Rice, I made a character loosely based off of Kayman; he had a lot of tens in dots. I told the ST that, I had to play him with philosophy in mind. I couldn't get wipey. I had to solve problems without resorting to walking over, holding the younger-vampire and simply waiting for the sun to rise. When I got Mummy:Revised, I like that system better given their other virtues such as memory etc. and I reworked my AntiDiluvian into a mummy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-10T04:43:05-07:00","id":1552261,"title":"","content":"Short answer is: No, I haven't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-11T19:12:06-07:00","id":1552295,"title":"","content":"Always.<br /> <br /> When this beasts uses their influence through their childer, the methuselahs use their influence through theirs and so on. So indirectly I have to know that the Antediluvians are up to and sometimes my PCs get a glimpse of their influence without entirely knowing what's truly going on but they know someone over them is watching and manipulating them.<br /> <br /> During a Sixth Age KotE chronicle they got to know Saulot's Hun and P'o separately as he is currently trying to become the Demon Emperor.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-14T17:38:37-07:00","id":1552394,"title":"","content":"Nope. The closest I've gotten is running a modified Chaos Factor for a VtM campaign, complete with its end boss Shaitan/Huitzilopchtli/Nergal. (Who's be as close to an antediluvian as anyone should ever want to encounter.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-15T16:34:05-07:00","id":1552431,"title":"","content":"I had Helen show up in a Chicago game, she had woken a few years before and was thought to be a neonate, the coterie was trying to help her out thinking she was newly embraced, showing her the &quot;ropes&quot; but she was learning about the world. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1680-justicar-seth","name":"Justicar-Seth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1680_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-17T11:18:48-07:00","id":1552501,"title":"","content":"Well, yes. We ran the <b>Giovanni Chronicles</b> (met Ashur-called-Cappadocius) and most of <b>Transylvania Chronicles</b>, which led my troupe to run into Tremere (an 'almost' Antediluvian) twice, not to mention gaining the attention of Absimiliard. Those encounters all left my players shook. During the latter stories, the troupe took a side trip to the resting place of the Eldest of the Tzimisce and played out the drama of Kupala's Night; Lambach's statements should be backed up by one of our player characters if it ever came to that. That, in turn, led them to have had a vision of Lambach's encounter with the Eldest under New York City (as presented in <b>Nights of Prophesy</b>). On the eve of Gehenna, they met a decrepit Augustus Giovani in the broken ruins of Kaymakli.<br /> <br /> Through all of these, my players were scared for their characters.<br /> <br /> Note that we have three timelines running in our twenty-plus-year long chronicle \u2014 a Dark Ages group, a conspiracy in the seventeenth century, and a coterie in the Final Nights \u2014 so not all of the above happened to the same characters of the same clans at the same power levels. There is also a decent bit of overlap where a member of the Elder Conspiracy may meet a member of the Younger Conspiracy and the like.<br /> <br /> My take has been that <i>IF</i> I am going to add such a creature to our game, it must be a big deal. something deserving of the weight of such a being. When we played through the Week of Nightmares (from <b>Time of the Thin Blood</b>), our Malkavian had a dream that she was the Ravnos ancient, and we played out some of what happened to that monster in a fairy-tale kind of way. It was the first taste of the <i>JYHAD</i> that my players got, and it has stuck with them.<br /> <br /> ...I've also had a few of Lilith's Apostates (from <b>Gehenna</b> hardcover) appear, without stating that they <i>MUST</i> be Antediluvian monsters. My players think they know who Mekhet, Lucian, Ikopabe, and Eikos are, but they are wrong. I don't know when I'll tell them the truth, if ever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-18T08:55:14-07:00","id":1552514,"title":"","content":"Had Malkav and Tzimisce in different games. Very fun, very useful, but mostly half asleep. Great cosmic horror.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This is me, just forgot my PW and changed my email<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25163-crytash2","name":"Crytash2","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25163_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}